cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or the results it reproduces, please cite the manuscripts below."
title: "Brane cluster gases: verification suite, figure scripts and audit of the ultraviolet-finite theory"
abstract: >-
  Source, verification suites and figure scripts for three manuscripts by Deep
  Bhattacharjee and Ushashi Bhattacharya. The
  first, "Brane cluster gases and ghost-free form factors for quantum gravity",
  comes with a suite of 176 independent checks in eleven groups, covering the
  residue sum rule, the pole dichotomy, the power counting, the Poisson
  generating functional, the Euclidean propagator of the Gaussian form factor,
  the weak-field threshold, the Schwinger parametric representation, and the
  composition of transmission amplitudes through a stack of branes. The second,
  "Perturbative finiteness of gravity in a scale-invariant gas of branes"
  (new in 2.0.0, retitled in 3.1.0 and 3.4.0), comes with
  195 Python, 84 C and 114 Julia checks of its analytical results, 17 Lean 4
  theorems on its power counting and five independent audit scripts (3.1.0): the single-brane factor of the
  cell model, the form factor of one realization of a Poisson gas of branes and
  its fluctuations, the necessity of fine graining, the vertex bound and power
  counting, the one-loop poles of the quartic operators, the vacuum energy, the
  one-loop bubble and its cutting rule, the free-field curvature and the
  Newtonian potential. The third, "Ghosts in Poisson Brane Gases" (new in
  3.0.0), computes the gas-averaged propagator exactly and determines the
  sign of its spectrum; it comes with 19 Python, 5 C and 9 Julia checks and
  13 Lean 4 theorems.
